Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:02.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Remember the budget of the shoebox.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.80,0:00:05.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Snapshot by snapshot,\Nenergy rises or falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.91,0:00:11.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Only the crowd balances, on average,\Nlike a bank account over the years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.90,0:00:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now, a tempting fix for the machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.35,0:00:19.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Force every generated snapshot to balance\Nits budget exactly. Better, or worse?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.61,0:00:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.05,0:00:27.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Push each snapshot until\Nits energy stops changing:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.62,0:00:30.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}the wide pile collapses\Ninto a spike at zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.07,0:00:33.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A ledger where every single day balances.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.04,0:00:36.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}No real account looks like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.25,0:00:41.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The {\c&H00A1ED&}distribution distance{\c&HF7F4F2&}\Nto the truth grows ninefold.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.39,0:00:44.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A short proof says why:\Neven a perfect generator,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.01,0:00:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}forced this way, cannot match the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.27,0:00:51.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So the budget goes on the crowd shelf.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.18,0:00:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}On the next test bench, a cruder\Nscore is fooled by such a spike.
